 This install applies to "Hard Drivin'" (c) 1989/1990 Tengen/Atari/Domark.
 Version 4.0b (13.10.2026)

 Requirements:
 -------------
 An original copy of the game and WHDLoad version 16.5 or later are required.
 WHDLoad must be accessible in the command path.

 The installed program requires 0.5 MB ChipMem and 1.0 MB OtherMem.
 Additional memory is needed to preload the game files. PRELOAD is recommended
 to avoid repeated disk access. An A1200 with Fast RAM is recommended for
 enhanced gameplay.

 The game requires an A500 Kickstart 1.3 image named "kick34005.A500" in
 "Devs:Kickstarts", together with "kick34005.A500.RTB". The image can be
 extracted from an A500 with GrabKick or a similar tool from Aminet.
 An incorrect or altered image will be rejected by WHDLoad. The RTB file
 is available in "util/boot/skick346.lha" on Aminet.

 Supported editions:
 - Original release
 - TNT compilation (same disk as Toobin')
 - Wheels Of Fire compilation (same disk as Chase HQ)
 - ReSpray budget release
 - Racing Masters compilation

 The new enhancements have been tested with the original SPS 0126 edition.
 The other supported editions retain their existing patches. Action 5,
 Summer Smashers and Sport Games Hits editions remain unverified.

 Installation:
 -------------
 Extract the package, double-click "Install" and follow the prompts.
 Select the game edition, destination drawer and preferred icon. Existing
 support for floppy disks and disk images is retained. Installing from disk
 images requires the additional tools described by the installer's help.
 For Wheels Of Fire, select the file named "2" (49804 bytes) when requested.
 The installer creates a HardDrivin drawer with the game files in "data".

 Features:
 ---------
 Start the game from its icon. Steering and menus use the mouse.
 High scores are loaded from and saved to hard disk.

 Keys:
   Q       Abort the current race.
   Esc/F10 Quit to Workbench. F10 is the default WHDLoad QuitKey, which can
           be changed with the QuitKey tooltype.

 CUSTOM2 controls the existing frame delay: 0 gives maximum rendering speed;
 higher values slow rendering down.

 Enhanced beta build:
 The enhanced build provides elapsed-time-based movement, physics, traffic
 and replay timing, allowing smoother rendering on accelerated Amigas.
 On 68020 and faster CPUs, physics can update every PAL field (50 times per
 second); the renderer draws as often as it can. On 68000, physics updates
 follow rendered frames. The original handling, including its abrupt skids,
 is retained. Original race-clock behaviour is also retained.

 In the enhanced build, use CUSTOM1=1 to enable the new simulation and
 CUSTOM2=0 for maximum rendering speed. CUSTOM1=0 selects original timing.
 Rendering options are selected with CUSTOM3:
   0  Original renderer (recommended for 68030).
   2  Optimized rotations (recommended for 68040/68060).
   6  Optimized rotations and blitter waits (recommended for 68000 and
      68020 with Fast RAM).

 These options currently require the enhanced build; a plain source build
 retains the original gameplay. Automatic selection of enhancements is not
 yet integrated. Full-lap checks and intro optimization remain deferred.

 History:
 --------
 version 4.0b (13.10.2026) done by Vesa Halttunen:
 - added optional frame-rate-independent simulation for the SPS 0126 edition,
   allowing smoother gameplay on faster Amigas while retaining original handling
 - adapted traffic, replays and related animation and sound timing to the
   enhanced simulation
 - added optional rendering optimizations for supported CPU configurations
 - updated the installer using the WHDLoad Install Template, retaining all
   five game editions and seven icon choices

 version 3.0 (23.03.2024) done by JOTD:
 - fixed keyboard on version SPS0126 (issue #0006342)
 - source code reworked & available
 
 version 2.04 (06/2008) done by Girv:
 - fixed crash bug when saving high scores (introduced with 2.03)

 v 2.03    03/2008
      - supports Racing Masters compilation version
      - upgraded installer script to latest version
      - added some new icons
      - requires WHDLoad v16.5+
 v 2.02    01/2005
      - supports ReSpray budget version
 v 2.01    01/2005
      - supports TNT compilation version
      - supports Wheels Of Fire compilation version
 v 2.00    12/2004
      - rewritten to use Kickstart emulation
      - fixed blthog usage
      - fixed access errors
      - fixed more cpu dependent delay loops
      - fixed self modifying graphics code
      - WHDLoad v16.0 compatible
      - uses standard release numbering system
      - uses standard WHDLoad installer script
 v 0801.1  08/2001
      - uses OSEmu 20010818
      - version checks moved from installer script into slave
      - miscellaneous installer script improvements
      - fixed cpu dependent delay loops

 v 0601.1  06/2001
      - fixed file loading crash bug
 
 v 0501.1  05/2001
      - first release
      - fixed to run with fastram and caches
      - fixed gear selection bug
      - fixed access violation
      - added high score loading/saving
      - added framerate control
      - added "abort game" key

